s the Olympic catamaran class. The class had a trapeze which allowed crew members to hook onto the wire and balance on the outside of the hull to keep the boat flatter. In 2000 a second trapeze was added to the design."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Only 14 boats entered this event which was won easily by the British crew of " [:a {:href "/athletes/64147"} "Reg White"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/63202"} "John Osborn"] ". They won four of the first six races and did not have to start the final race to win the gold medal. They had been the clear favorites, having won the recent World Championships and five different international regattas within the last year. The American silver medalists, " [:a {:href "/athletes/62957"} "David McFaull"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/63502"} "Mike Rothwell"] ", raced out of Hawai’i, where McFaull worked as a disc jockey."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Net Points"] [:th {} "Total Points"] [:th {} "Race #1"] [:th {} "Race #2"] [:th {} "Race #3"] [:th {} "Race #4"] [:th {} "Race #5"] [:th {} "Race #6"] [:th {} "Race #7"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "Great Britain"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "18.0"] [:td {} "38.0"] [:td {} ".0 (1)"] [:td {} ".0 (1)"] [:td {} "10.0 (5)"] [:td {} ".0 (1)"] [:td {} "8.0 (4)"] [:td {} ".0 (1)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "17"} [:a {:href "/athletes/63202"} "John Osborn"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/64147"} "Reg White"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} "United States"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.